  "caption": "Quinn's new accessory: crutches. By day two the armpits were sore, and the coffee did not survive.\n\nYour weight should go through your hands, not your armpits. Crutch tops usually sit two to three finger-widths below the armpit, with grips at wrist height and elbows slightly bent.\n\nTips that often help: move the crutches and sore leg together, then step through with the good leg; on stairs, up with the good, down with the bad; carry things in a small backpack; clear rugs and cords; and rest before your arms tire. Always follow your team's weight-bearing advice.\n\nTingling or numbness in your hands, trouble coping at home, or increasing leg pain is worth raising with your team.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
